00:32:51,940 --> 00:32:53,940
of how far ahead they're working,

343
00:32:53,940 --> 00:32:56,940
sort of fetching forward and future instructions

344
00:32:56,940 --> 00:32:59,940
while finishing up the ones that still remain.

345
00:32:59,940 --> 00:33:04,160
So that's my ocean line or my tanker analogy.

346
00:33:04,160 --> 00:33:06,160
But all of a sudden you come, and then

347
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:09,230
And then what happens when they hit a branch,

348
00:33:09,230 --> 00:33:12,230
they'll try to guess, it's called branch prediction,

349
00:33:12,230 --> 00:33:15,230
and guess, where is this branch going to go,

350
00:33:15,230 --> 00:33:18,230
where, you know, will the conditional branch be taken,

351
00:33:18,230 --> 00:33:20,230
or is it going to fall through?

352
00:33:20,230 --> 00:33:21,230
And they're pretty good at that.

353
00:33:21,230 --> 00:33:25,230
They're good at it 98% of the time.

354
00:33:25,230 --> 00:33:30,260
So they can even anticipate sort of curves in the road,

355
00:33:30,260 --> 00:33:33,420
my analogy is breaking down,

356
00:33:33,420 --> 00:33:35,420
and start going in that direction.

357
00:33:35,420 --> 00:33:40,420
going in that direction and as long as they get it right, it's very efficient.

